ess-and-intensity]])\n  | \n  | [F3] Every locally finite translation-invariant Borel measure $m$ on $\\mathbb R^d$ satisfies $m(B)=m(Q)\\lambda_d(B)$. ([[lem-translation-invariant-locally-finite-borel-measure-on-rd]])\n  | \n  | \n  | \n  | **Given:** AC, Countable Choice, a stationary point process $\\eta$ with $\\rho=\\mathbb E\\eta(Q)\\in(0,\\infty)$, and its mean measure $\\nu$.\n  | \n  | 1.1 By [F1], $\\nu(B)=\\mathbb E[\\eta(B)]$ is a Borel measure, and $\\nu(Q)=\\rho$. [given, F1, F2]\n  | \n  | 1.2 For any Borel $B$ and translation $x$, the definition of recentering gives\n  | \n  | 2.1 Let $B$ be bounded Borel. Choose an integer $n$ with $B\\subseteq[-n,n)^d$. This cube is a finite disjoint union of translates $Q+k$, $k\\in\\{-n,\\ldots,n-1\\}^d$. Stationarity [F2] gives $\\nu(Q+k)=\\mathbb E[\\eta(Q+k)]=\\rho$ for every such $k$. Monotonicity and finite additivity therefore give $\\nu(B)\\le(2n)^d\\rho<\\infty$. Hence $\\nu$ is locally finite. [step 1.1, F2, algebra]\n  | $$\\nu(B+x)=\\mathbb E[\\eta(B+x)]=\\mathbb E[(\\theta_x\\eta)(B)]=\\mathbb E[\\eta(B)]=\\nu(B),$$\n  | where the third equality is stationarity [F2]. Thus $\\nu$ is translation invariant. [step 1.1, F2]\n  | \n  | 3.1 Apply [F3] to the locally finite translation-invariant measure $\\nu$. Since $\\nu(Q)=\\rho$ by step 1.1, it follows that $\\nu(B)=\\rho\\lambda_d(B)$ for every Borel $B$. This is the claimed mean-measure formula. [A1, A2, step 1.1, step 2.1, step 1.2, F3] ∎\nPASS items/thm-stratified-interference-variance-estimators-conservative.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-stratified-total-unbiasedness-and-variance.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-subgaussian-mixture-confidence-sequence.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-survival-cumulative-hazard-identity.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-truncated-normal-selective-pivot-is-conditionally-uniform.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-two-stage-expansion-total-unbiasedness-and-variance.md (direct)\nPASS items/thm-two-stage-randomized-interference-estimators-unbiased.md (direct)\nREPAIR items/thm-van-hove-window-average-l2-consistency.md: passes only after auto-repair — adopt the canonical form:\n  | **Given:** $d\\ge1$, a probability space $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$, a\n  | jointly measurable real field $X:\\mathbb R^d\\times\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$,\n  | $\\mathbb E[X(s)]=\\mu$, $\\mathbb E[X(s)^2]<\\infty$ for every $s$, stationary\n  | covariance $C(t-s)$, $\\int_{\\mathbb R^d}|C(h)|\\,dh<\\infty$, and a Van Hove\n  | sequence $(W_n)$.\n  | \n  | [A1] [[def-van-hove-window-sequence]]: under $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$,\n  | [[thm-borel-sets-are-lebesgue-measurable]] makes every Borel $W_n$\n  | Lebesgue measurable and [[thm-lebesgue-measure-is-a-complete-measure]]\n  | supplies Lebesgue measure; every $W_n$ has finite positive volume,\n  | $|W_n|\\to\\infty$, and for each compact $K$,\n  | $|(W_n+K)\\setminus W_n|/|W_n|\\to0$.\n  | \n  | [A2] [[def-spatial-window-average]]: when a sample path is Lebesgue integrable,\n  | $\\bar X_{W_n}=|W_n|^{-1}\\int_{W_n}X(s)\\,ds$.\n  | \n  | [F1] [[def-random-field-stationarity-covariance-and-variogram]],\n  | [[def-random-element-and-real-random-variable]], and\n  | [[def-borel-sigma-algebra]]: a field is a family of real random variables on\n  | one probability space; joint measurability is an additional hypothesis for\n  | spatial integration, and wide stationarity supplies a constant mean and\n  | displacement-indexed covariance.\n  | \n  | [F2] [[def-moments-variance-and-covariance]]: variance is the expected\n  | centered square and covariance is the expected centered product; symmetry makes\n  | the reverse-lag convention in the Given equivalent to the supplier covariance\n  | convention.\n  | \n  | [F3] [[def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable]]:\n  | expectation is the Lebesgue integral against $\\mathbb P$.\n  | \n  | [F4] [[cor-cauchy-schwarz-for-random-variables]]: for $U,V\\in L^2(\\mathbb P)$,\n  | $\\mathbb E|UV|\\le\\|U\\|_2\\|V\\|_2$.\n  | \n  |